    "body": "That would definitely be useful. I'll add some commits to this PR for that, but I'm still unsure about the following:\r\n\r\n- Instead of specifying just a single battery state for the `when` clause, what about implementing it as a list so the same style can be applied to multiple battery states?\r\n- Besides `charging` and `discharging`, the `State` enum also has types like `empty` or `full`. Maybe we could use this enum for the config field? It could be implemented as an `Option` so that a missing field (`None`) would apply the display config to all states.",
    "created_at": "2022-04-15T19:46:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-15T20:04:31Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/3849#discussion_r851462140",
